{
  "$description": "frontiers-figures' figure roles (spec FR-004, FR-005): what each figure class colors, and, per variant, the brand role or mix of roles it takes (\"text!62!surface\" is 62% text, 38% surface, as xcolor writes it). A figure's source names roles by class (f-<role> for fill, s-<role> for stroke, c-<role> for a gradient stop) and never a color; theme.py turns this table and a brand into the stylesheet a consumer puts in the figure. Layout variants change the canvas, never a color. series: a chart's categorical roles, each 3:1 against the background and, in the color variants, distinct to normal and color-blind vision (spec FR-012). sequential: a scale's steps, ordered from least to most.",
